{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8bc68f27-747c-48a2-b7cb-0c962ca4e6c1",
    "name": "Electronics Hub — Public Product API v1",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "Import this collection AND catalog-public-api-v1.postman_environment.json, then select the Electronics Hub environment.\n\nSet base_url to your application origin, including http:// or https://, without /api/v1/catalog or a trailing slash. Use HTTPS in production.\n\nThe API is anonymous. No bearer token, login, database username, or password belongs in Postman.\n\nServer prerequisite: Catalog enabled, CATALOG_PUBLIC_API_ENABLED=true, and a separate SELECT-only public API database account configured. API_UNAVAILABLE (503) means server configuration must be checked.\n\nRun the collection once in its saved order with a 1500 ms delay. It covers all 10 GET endpoints plus parts query examples and four expected 422/404 errors.\n\nTree fills empty category_path, series_path, resolve_path and search_term variables from real catalog data. Parts fills empty part_search from a returned SKU. Facets fills an empty filter_key and sample values using public non-file facets. Existing paths are preserved; set auto_discover=false for manual control. Clear derived variables when changing server/catalog.\n\nPaths must be raw slash-separated resource.path values from Tree, without a leading slash; scripts encode segments and query values. Requests requiring unavailable data are skipped with a Postman Console message. Empty catalogs cannot exercise data-dependent endpoints.\n\nTo inspect a different series, set series_path and clear part_search, filter_key, filter_value and filter_value_2, then rerun Parts and Facets.\n\nDefault limits: 60 requests/minute/IP overall, 20/minute search, 30/minute parts/facets. Repeated runs may receive 429; respect Retry-After.\n\nTests verify status, JSON envelope, correlation ID, cache/security headers and endpoint response shapes. They do not replace backend visibility/security regression tests.\n\nPostman scripting reference: https://learning.postman.com/docs/tests-and-scripts/write-scripts/postman-sandbox-reference/pm-execution/"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const base = String(pm.variables.get(\"base_url\") || \"\").trim().replace(/\\/+$/, \"\");",
          "if (!/^https?:\\/\\/[^/?#\\s]+$/.test(base)) {",
          "    throw new Error(\"Set base_url in the selected Electronics Hub environment to your application origin (http/https, no /api path).\");",
          "}",
          "pm.variables.set(\"base_url\", base);",
          "for (const key of [\"category_path\", \"series_path\", \"resolve_path\"]) {",
          "    const path = String(pm.variables.get(key) || \"\");",
          "    pm.variables.set(key + \"_encoded\", path.split(\"/\").map(encodeURIComponent).join(\"/\"));",
          "}",
          "for (const key of [\"search_term\", \"part_search\", \"filter_key\", \"filter_value\", \"filter_value_2\", \"sort\", \"direction\"]) {",
          "    pm.variables.set(key + \"_encoded\", encodeURIComponent(String(pm.variables.get(key) || \"\")));",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "pm.test(\"Response is JSON\", function () {",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"Content-Type\") || \"\").to.match(/application\\/json/i);",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an(\"object\");",
          "});",
          "pm.test(\"Response has safe cache and content headers\", function () {",
          "    const cache = pm.response.headers.get(\"Cache-Control\") || \"\";",
          "    pm.expect(cache).to.include(\"no-store\");",
          "    pm.expect(cache).to.include(\"private\");",
          "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get(\"X-Content-Type-Options\")).to.equal(\"nosniff\");",
          "});",
          "pm.test(\"Correlation ID matches response header\", function () {",
          "    const body = pm.response.json();",
          "    pm.expect(body.correlationId).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty;",
          "    pm.expect(body.correlationId).to.equal(pm.response.headers.get(\"X-Correlation-ID\"));",
          "});",
          "pm.test(\"Response uses the public API envelope\", function () {",
          "    const body = pm.response.json();",
          "    if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
          "        pm.expect(body.success).to.equal(true);",
          "        pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"data\");",
          "    } else {",
          "        pm.expect(body.success).to.equal(false);",
          "        pm.expect(body.errorCode).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty;",
          "        pm.expect(body.message).to.be.a(\"string\").and.not.empty;",
          "        pm.expect(body).to.have.property(\"details\");",
          "    }",
          "});",
          "if (pm.response.code === 503) {",
          "    console.warn(\"API unavailable: check Catalog module, CATALOG_PUBLIC_API_ENABLED and the separate SELECT-only database account on the server. Do not add database credentials to Postman.\");",
          "}",
          "if (pm.response.code === 429) {",
          "    console.warn(\"Rate limited. Wait for Retry-After and rerun once with a 1500 ms request delay.\");",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
